      "margin_number": null,
      "speaker": null,
      "text": "(a) All gen. plurals end in -ων.\n(b) Gen. singulars of type 3 nouns/adjectives all originally ended in -ος.\nLater contractions and other changes gave rise to forms in -ους and -εως.\n(c) Gen. singulars in types 1 and 2 nouns/adjectives end (masculine)\nin -ου and (feminine) in -ης (1a, 1c) or -ας (1b). Remind yourself of the\nrules for these nouns (especially the ι ρ ε rule) at 56-57.\n(d) 1d nouns like ναύτης, νεανίας are tricky: ναύτης, νεανίας is their\nnom. form (not feminine gen. s.!) and their gen. s. is ναύτου, νεανίου.",
      "lang": "mixed",
      "para_no": null,
      "marker": "black_right_pointing_triangle",
      "table": null,
      "exercise": null,
      "caption": null,
